    "directo": {"en": "direct (feminine: directa)", "pron": "di-REK-to / di-REK-ta", "cat": "adjective"},
    "cancelado": {"en": "cancelled (feminine: cancelada)", "pron": "kan-se-LA-do / kan-se-LA-da", "cat": "adjective"}
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "At the ticket office"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "To buy: **Un billete de ida y vuelta para Sevilla, por favor.**\n\nTo ask about a route: **¿A qué hora sale** el próximo tren? **¿A qué hora llega?** **¿De qué andén sale?** **¿Cuánto tarda?** **¿Es directo?** **¿Hay que hacer transbordo?**\n\nTimetables use the present: el tren **sale** a las diez y **llega** a las doce. **Tarda** dos horas. On a timetable, **salida** is departure and **llegada** is arrival. These are scheduled times; delays can change them.\n\nA late train **lleva** or **tiene** veinte minutos **de retraso**.\n\nAt the airport, **facturas** (check) your luggage, find **la puerta de embarque** and check whether **el vuelo está cancelado**. **Directo** agrees with the noun: el tren es directo; la conexión es directa."
      }
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": {"en": "At the station"},
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Un billete para Sevilla, por favor.",
          "en": "A ticket to Seville, please.",
          "analisis": [["Un billete", "object"], ["para Sevilla", "destination"], ["por favor", "politeness"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Empleado",
          "es": "¿Solo ida o ida y vuelta?",
          "en": "One way or return?",
          "analisis": [["¿Solo ida", "option"], ["ida y vuelta", "option"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "De ida y vuelta. ¿A qué hora sale el próximo tren?",
          "en": "Return. What time does the next train leave?",
          "analisis": [["De ida y vuelta", "type"], ["¿A qué hora", "question"], ["sale", "verb"], ["el próximo tren", "subject"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Empleado",
          "es": "Sale a las diez y llega a las doce y media.",
          "en": "It leaves at ten and arrives at half past twelve.",
          "analisis": [["Sale", "verb"], ["a las diez", "time"], ["llega", "verb"], ["a las doce y media", "time"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "¿De qué andén sale?",
          "en": "Which platform does it leave from?",
          "analisis": [["¿De qué andén", "question"], ["sale", "verb"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Empleado",
          "es": "Del andén cuatro. Hoy lleva diez minutos de retraso.",
          "en": "From platform four. Today it's ten minutes late.",
          "analisis": [["Del andén cuatro", "place"], ["Hoy", "time"], ["lleva", "verb"], ["diez minutos de retraso", "object"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "titulo": {"en": "Example timetable (for practice)"},
      "frases": [
        {"es": "MADRID → TOLEDO | Salida 10:15 | Llegada 10:48 | Andén 6", "en": "MADRID → TOLEDO | Departure 10:15 | Arrival 10:48 | Platform 6", "analisis": [["Salida", "departure"], ["Llegada", "arrival"], ["Andén 6", "platform"]]},
        {"es": "TOLEDO → MADRID | Salida 12:20 | Llegada 12:53 | Andén 2", "en": "TOLEDO → MADRID | Departure 12:20 | Arrival 12:53 | Platform 2", "analisis": [["Salida", "departure"], ["Llegada", "arrival"], ["Andén 2", "platform"]]},
        {"es": "Aviso: El tren de las 10:15 sale con 15 minutos de retraso.", "en": "Notice: The 10:15 train is leaving 15 minutes late.", "analisis": [["Aviso", "notice"], ["sale con 15 minutos de retraso", "is delayed"]]}
      ]
    },
    {"tipo": "vocabulario"},
